{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Legislate to ensure second hand cars remain affordable for ordinary people.",
        "additional_details": "The soaring cost of used vehicles prices working people out of essential transit. Public transport is often non-existent, making a private car necessary for jobs and childcare. High dealer fees, software locks, and a corporate culture of planned failure artificially drive up prices. Protecting independent garages and guaranteeing parts availability will lower repair costs and keep cars affordable.",
        "background": "\u2022 Open OBD2 diagnostic and part coding.\r\n    \u2022 Mandate 10-year transferable warranties.\r\n    \u2022 Enforce service schedules that promote longevity.\r\n    \u2022 Ban proprietary fastenings.\r\n    \u2022 Standardise VED to a flat rate.",
